# Nix-free dependency pinning for LatticeWM, managed by qlot.
#
# flake.nix pins these libraries through nixpkgs, which is exact but only
# available where Nix is. This file is the equivalent pin for a plain SBCL on
# any distribution: a Quicklisp dist version fixes every library in that dist
# to one specific release, so the set resolved here does not drift.
#
# Every system flake.nix lists is present in this dist -- alexandria, cffi,
# cffi-grovel, babel, closer-mop, plump, array-utils, documentation-utils,
# trivial-indent, trivial-features, trivial-gray-streams, bordeaux-threads,
# fiveam, swank (via the slime release), and wayflan. There is no out-of-dist
# git dependency to track separately, so this one line covers all of them.
#
#   qlot install          -> installs the pinned set into .qlot/ and writes
#                            qlfile.lock
#   qlot exec sbcl        -> a REPL seeing exactly those versions
#
# qlfile.lock is NOT yet committed. Generating it requires a working `qlot
# install', which failed in the environment where this file was written: SBCL
# could not resolve beta.quicklisp.org through sb-bsd-sockets under WSL, dying
# with "The value of SB-BSD-SOCKETS::ADDRESS is (NIL NIL)". curl reached the
# same host, so this is an SBCL name-resolution problem rather than a fault in
# this file. Run `qlot install' on a normal Linux machine and commit the
# resulting qlfile.lock alongside this file.
#
# Bump deliberately by changing the date below and re-running `qlot install',
# never by letting it float.
dist quicklisp 2026-01-01
